      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Oxygen-dependent metabolism of neutrophils and monocytes and antioxidant defense and heparin and trimetasidine effects on them were studied in 39 patients with unstable angina. All the patients showed a significant activation of neutrophils and monocytes by NBT-test, insignificant one by chemiluminescence in active serum superoxide dismutase and reduced total antioxidative serum potential. There was also a moderate rise in the level of CIC in enhanced HBT-test. Heparin in unstable angina pectoris produced stimulation of oxygen-dependent metabolism of neutrophils and monocytes, ischemic damage to the myocardium was not changed. This was observed after treatment with preductal indicating antioxidant properties of this drug."},
